  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the primary partner for the Vietnam Australia Centre (VAC), Ho Chi Minh National Academy of Politics (HCMA) made considerable improvements in its governance through VAC activities, including transparency, efficiency, strategic vision, and responsiveness to policy advisory activities.  
&#x200d;
 Participants from HCMA, both central and regional academies have enhanced their knowledge on core leadership competencies, inclusive management, professional reflection, gender equality in leadership, strategic analysis and analytical writing through training courses provided by HCMA.  
&#x200d;
 Australia, through the VAC, has also supported HCMA with strategic research projects including the Women in Leadership Index, and&#x202f;policy briefs and recommendation papers for the 40-year Doi Moi review activity in preparation for the 14th National Party Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aus4Skills achieved various milestones in 2024 which strengthened vocational education and training (VET) systems in Vietnam:
&#x200d;
Informing National VET Policy: Aus4Skills provided technical assistance to Government of Vietnam and VET colleges and contributed to two Government circulars that provided nationwide guidance on VET curriculum development (Circular 01/2024) and VET standards and accreditation (Circular 14/2024).
&#x200d;
Pioneering Industry Foresight: Vietnam&apos;s inaugural industry skills forecast for the port sector (2024-2028) and an updated forecast for logistics (2024-2026) were launched in 2024 with the technical assistance of Aus4Skills. These forecasts, developed with insights from local business and industry partners, introduced skills development practices to inform decisions of Government of Vietnam, industry and colleges on their future skills needs and investments.
&#x200d;
Boosting Graduates&#x2019; Employability and Job Readiness: Aus4Skills supported VET colleges to apply the competency-based training and assessment approach in curriculum development and training delivery and to promote industry linkages. A program case study in 2024 confirmed the importance of strong college-enterprise linkages, leading to improved alignment between graduates&#x2019; competencies and industry expectations, enhancing graduates&#x2019; employability and job readiness. 93.3% of surveyed employers found the newly recruited employees from Aus4Skills partner colleges met their requirements, and 83.7% of graduates felt well-prepared for future careers.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aus4Skills continued to promote VET as a career pathway for people with disabilities and consulted with its OPD network in this effort.
&#x200d;
Key personnel of the Center for Disability Research and Capacity Development (DRD) participated in technical logistics and teacher training courses supported by Aus4Skills with other VET stakeholders. These courses helped build VET- and logistics-related technical capacity for DRD and enabled them to identify opportunities and challenges faced by students and employees with disabilities in the logistics sector. DRD was then engaged by Aus4Skills as a disability inclusion resource partner to provide support for VET colleges and promote vocational training and career opportunities for people with disabilities. This support included training, design of approach to support students with disabilities, mentoring and coaching implementation of action plans by VET colleges.
&#x200d;
  
&#x200d;
In 2023, 32 VET educators attended DRD training on supporting students with disabilities.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Vietnam Australia Centre (VAC) is strengthening the capacity of its partners through knowledge sharing initiatives and contributing to enhanced governance mechanisms.  In 2024 the VAC organised a workshop for members of the Vietnamese Prime Minister&apos;s Advisory Council on Administrative Procedures Reform. Nearly a hundred officials at Director General and Deputy Director General level from 11 ministries, as well as representatives from business and socio-political organisations met with Australian experts and discussed reform mechanisms, policies and administrative procedures to improve the business environment and facilitate trade and production.
&#x200d;
Following the workshop, two Australian experts were invited to produce an independent report on &#x201c;Reforming mechanisms, policies and administrative procedures in investment and labour&#x201d;. The report assessed the implementation of administrative procedures in Vietnam&#x2019;s investment and labour areas and provided Australian experience and recommendations to improve the enabling environment for production, business and investment in Vietnam. This report will inform the Advisory Council&#x2019;s future recommendation for reform in investment licensing, labour and insurance.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disability equity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the Aus4Skills program, various Organisations of Persons with Disabilities (OPDs) in Vietnam have initiated impactful &#x201c;application projects&#x201d; following participation in skill development.
&#x200d;
Can Tho OPD developed a strategic plan for the inclusion of people with disabilities in the logistics sector and organised workshops to promote the competency-based training and assessment approach, shared foundational logistics knowledge and fostered inclusion of and understanding for LGBTI individuals and people with disabilities through gender equality campaigns.
&#x200d;
Hanoi OPD applied systematic monitoring and evaluation to better understand and address the psychological barriers faced by young people with disabilities seeking employment, leading to more tailored support and improved job-seeking skills. They also contributed to international dialogues on human trafficking and disseminated knowledge on professional development and logistics inclusion to other OPDs. Hanoi OPD also introduced startup and capacity-building programs to help women with disabilities achieve more stable livelihoods.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
